1. Logical Address to Physical Address Using Base and Limit Registers
Aim

To simulate the translation of a logical address into a physical address using base and limit registers.

Algorithm
Read the base address and limit value.
Read the logical address.
Check whether the logical address is less than the limit.
If valid, calculate:
Physical Address = Base Address + Logical Address
Otherwise, display an invalid address message.

C Program

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int base, limit, logical, physical;

    printf("Enter Base Address: ");
    scanf("%d", &base);

    printf("Enter Limit: ");
    scanf("%d", &limit);

    printf("Enter Logical Address: ");
    scanf("%d", &logical);

    if (logical >= 0 && logical < limit) {
        physical = base + logical;

        printf("\nLogical Address: %d", logical);
        printf("\nPhysical Address: %d", physical);
        printf("\nAddress is Valid.\n");
    } else {
        printf("\nLogical Address: %d", logical);
        printf("\nAddress is Invalid. Memory access denied.\n");
    }

    return 0;
}

